{
New algorithm: For each bin, compute the remaining capacity after hypothetically adding the item, then assign higher priority to bins where the remaining capacity is minimized (closest to zero without going negative), and among those, break ties by preferring bins with larger original capacity.
}

{
New algorithm: For each bin, compute the ratio of the bin's remaining capacity after adding the item to the bin's original capacity, then assign higher priority to bins where this ratio is minimized (to leave more proportional space free), and among those, break ties by preferring bins with smaller original capacity.
}

{
New algorithm: For each bin, compute the ratio of the item size to the bin's remaining capacity after adding the item, then assign higher priority to bins where this ratio is maximized (filling proportion), and among those, break ties by preferring bins with larger original capacity.
